## R7 proof, check 3: a small sphere between a distant light and a large
## receiving sphere casts a visible shadow, plus an ambient light so the
## shadow itself is not pure black. shadow_nolight.rib (the distant light
## removed) and shadow_noblocker.rib (the small sphere removed) share this
## scene; tests/shadowrender_test.cpp pins one pixel against both -- inside
## the shadow it matches shadow_nolight.rib's render, and once the blocker
## is gone it reads brighter than that by more than GOLDEN_CHANNEL_TOL. Not
## third-party.
Display "shadow.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 320 240 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [45]
Clipping 0.5 50
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
LightSource "ambientlight" 1 "intensity" [0.1]
LightSource "distantlight" 2 "intensity" [1.0] "lightcolor" [1 1 1]
	"from" [5 2 -3] "to" [0 0 0]
Sides 1
Surface "matte" "Ka" [0.2] "Kd" [0.8]

AttributeBegin
	Translate 0 0 7
	Sphere 3 -3 3 360
AttributeEnd

AttributeBegin
	Translate 1.8 0.8 3.5
	Sphere 0.6 -0.6 0.6 360
AttributeEnd
WorldEnd
